(114868, 5140, 3102, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid I''m not too fond of the composition, and I''m a bit iffy on whether it meets the "candid" requirement.  Maybe if the dog''s expression, along with the ice cream, were visible, I''d rank it a little higher.</td>', 'I''m afraid I''m not too fond of the composition, and I''m a bit iffy on whether it meets the "candid" requirement.  Maybe if the dog''s expression, along with the ice cream, were visible, I''d rank it a little higher.', '2002-09-02 22:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114869, 5140, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background5,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,<br/>Total Averaged Rating5.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background5,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,Total Averaged Rating5.   Autool', '2002-09-03 10:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114870, 5140, 806, '<td valign="top">any second now he''s gonna leap....</td>', 'any second now he''s gonna leap....', '2002-09-03 10:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114871, 5140, 2204, '<td valign="top">These were some of the rules I set up for myself as I prepared for the candid challenge:<br/>The backs of heads or people are not candid.<br/>The subject cannot be very far away.<br/>Animals live by instinct or are trained to do certain things, they are not candid.<br/>Here with your entry you have broken all my rules.  This IS candid.  I can see from the stance and ears that this dog has something on his mind and it doesn''t have anything to do with his training.  Even if his instinct is telling him "this might be something good to eat" you have caught the instant between the thought and the deed.  Good job!!  Technically I think the photo needs some help, and for most challenges it would get lower scores for backgraound, set-up, angle, and lighting to name a few.  However, for candid it is great.  =7 syamjonimi ;''-D</td>', 'These were some of the rules I set up for myself as I prepared for the candid challenge:The backs of heads or people are not candid.The subject cannot be very far away.Animals live by instinct or are trained to do certain things, they are not candid.Here with your entry you have broken all my rules.  This IS candid.  I can see from the stance and ears that this dog has something on his mind and it doesn''t have anything to do with his training.  Even if his instinct is telling him "this might be something good to eat" you have caught the instant between the thought and the deed.  Good job!!  Technically I think the photo needs some help, and for most challenges it would get lower scores for backgraound, set-up, angle, and lighting to name a few.  However, for candid it is great.  =7 syamjonimi ;''-D', '2002-09-03 18:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114872, 5140, 3645, '<td valign="top">What kind of dog is that? Looks similar to my Rhodesian Ridgebacks''. Anyway, I know exactly what this dog is thinking. Now I know his perspective too. Good candid shot with nice color and focus. I like the fact that the ice cream (?) is right above the center of the dog''s head. No bones about it, you did a good job.</td>', 'What kind of dog is that? Looks similar to my Rhodesian Ridgebacks''. Anyway, I know exactly what this dog is thinking. Now I know his perspective too. Good candid shot with nice color and focus. I like the fact that the ice cream (?) is right above the center of the dog''s head. No bones about it, you did a good job.', '2002-09-03 21:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114873, 5140, 2932, '<td valign="top">mood captured - silly humans from a pet''s perspective<br/>sincerity of expressions - can''t see any faces; body language is average</td>', 'mood captured - silly humans from a pet''s perspectivesincerity of expressions - can''t see any faces; body language is average', '2002-09-04 01:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
