(114638, 5132, 2353, '<td valign="top">Excellent job!  Fits challenge perfectly to me...a candid shot that conveys emotion and has good photographic technique.  -KrazyKat</td>', 'Excellent job!  Fits challenge perfectly to me...a candid shot that conveys emotion and has good photographic technique.  -KrazyKat', '2002-09-03 14:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114639, 5132, 3280, '<td valign="top">Great shot!  I love the traffic in the background as I feel it actually adds to the photo instead of detracting from it.  He seems oblivious as the world is flying by.  Colors are great with him standing out from the grays.  Very nice, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Great shot!  I love the traffic in the background as I feel it actually adds to the photo instead of detracting from it.  He seems oblivious as the world is flying by.  Colors are great with him standing out from the grays.  Very nice, good luck in the challenge.', '2002-09-03 16:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114640, 5132, 51167, '<td valign="top">Good photo.</td>', 'Good photo.', '2002-09-04 03:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114641, 5132, 3469, '<td valign="top">Well-shot. I like the unsharpness of the busy background against the sharpness of the oblivious foreground figure.</td>', 'Well-shot. I like the unsharpness of the busy background against the sharpness of the oblivious foreground figure.', '2002-09-04 16:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114642, 5132, 2866, '<td valign="top">Very good.</td>', 'Very good.', '2002-09-04 22:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114643, 5132, 772, '<td valign="top">Very nice candid... The depth of field here is excellent.. It''s not too shallow and it makes your subject stand out nicely.  This is out of your control, but I wish the man was sitting about one foot further back :)  He''s a little too close to the center of the frame for my taste, but the barrell framing the right side of the image works very nicely.  good shot :) - 7 - jmsetzler</td>', 'Very nice candid... The depth of field here is excellent.. It''s not too shallow and it makes your subject stand out nicely.  This is out of your control, but I wish the man was sitting about one foot further back :)  He''s a little too close to the center of the frame for my taste, but the barrell framing the right side of the image works very nicely.  good shot :) - 7 - jmsetzler', '2002-09-05 12:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114644, 5132, 637, '<td valign="top">This is my idea of what a candid image ought ot be... Just close enough... just wide enough... captures the essence of the subject at this isolated moment in time.  7 sjgleah</td>', 'This is my idea of what a candid image ought ot be... Just close enough... just wide enough... captures the essence of the subject at this isolated moment in time.  7 sjgleah', '2002-09-05 16:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114645, 5132, 1993, '<td valign="top">Look at his cute little hair sticking out from under his hat!  Nice picture.  I like it a lot..it is growing on me.</td>', 'Look at his cute little hair sticking out from under his hat!  Nice picture.  I like it a lot..it is growing on me.', '2002-09-05 18:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114646, 5132, 3737, '<td valign="top">good candid capture</td>', 'good candid capture', '2002-09-05 20:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114647, 5132, 811, '<td valign="top">i love how he looks so peaceful and in solitude but in the background it looks so busy.  Good focus and lighting as well. karmat</td>', 'i love how he looks so peaceful and in solitude but in the background it looks so busy.  Good focus and lighting as well. karmat', '2002-09-06 13:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114648, 5132, 2247, '<td valign="top">Would have been a nice pic but you use Photoshop''s Fill Flash too much.  Your subject''s face is too ashen-grey.  I had the same problem.  Instead of Fill Flash, I use Lightness under Color (under Enhance) up to +10.  Then I go to Enhance again and use Contrast up 10+ and usually that will do the trick for brightening up your pics.  Good luck!</td>', 'Would have been a nice pic but you use Photoshop''s Fill Flash too much.  Your subject''s face is too ashen-grey.  I had the same problem.  Instead of Fill Flash, I use Lightness under Color (under Enhance) up to +10.  Then I go to Enhance again and use Contrast up 10+ and usually that will do the trick for brightening up your pics.  Good luck!', '2002-09-08 00:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(114649, 5132, 3127, '<td valign="top">What a wonderful photo!  I love the hues and content.</td>', 'What a wonderful photo!  I love the hues and content.', '2002-09-08 21:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
