(115084, 5158, 3469, '<td valign="top">I understand the problem: if you would have changed the standpoint to the level of the childrens faces they would no longer have been candid, but reacted to the camera. Consider shooting in the blind as I call it: just let your camera be at the end of your arm, free in your hand, at the place where your eye should have been. Point and shoot. It needs a little practice, but it makes for a  lot of real candid pictures. The current standpoint of the photographer is just not very appealing.</td>', 'I understand the problem: if you would have changed the standpoint to the level of the childrens faces they would no longer have been candid, but reacted to the camera. Consider shooting in the blind as I call it: just let your camera be at the end of your arm, free in your hand, at the place where your eye should have been. Point and shoot. It needs a little practice, but it makes for a  lot of real candid pictures. The current standpoint of the photographer is just not very appealing.', '2002-09-03 17:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
